    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Train Tree 2**\\n\\nGoal: Train a new tree on the (Fixed) dataset so you can compare it to Tree 1.\\n\\n1. Read the **Dataset Update** below.\\n2. In **Predict**, choose your label. In **Using**, keep your two features, or add more.\\n3. Write your label and features in the Tree 2 row of **Tree 1 vs. Tree 2** in your guide.\\n4. Click **Train model**.\\n\\nYou are done when your tree shows. Go to the **Testing** tab.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Dataset Update**: \\n\\nAdds three calm songs that have singing.\\n\\n**Data Source**: \\n\\nSpotify Tracks Dataset on Hugging Face\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**Train Tree 2**\\n\\nGoal: Train a new tree on the (Fixed) dataset so you can compare it to Tree 1.\\n\\n1. Copy your Tree 1 results from Lesson 12 into the Tree 1 row of **Tree 1 vs. Tree 2** in your guide. Your label is in **My Data**.\\n2. Find your **Accuracy** at the top. Write it in the Tree 2 row.\\n3. Click **Accuracy**. Write the **Correct** number in the Tree 2 row.\\n4. Add **Correct** and **Incorrect**. Write the total after \\\"out of\\\". Click **Back to Testing**.\\n5. Click **Save image** (the camera under your tree). Click **Save to Backpack**.\\n\\nYou are done when **Tree 1 vs. Tree 2** in your guide is full and Tree 2 is in your Backpack.\"\r\n}",
